# Figma component guidelines

Use the New Editor Blocks / Material 3 components. Do not invent a parallel control language.

## Text field (outlined)

- Width 282px, height 40px, 1px `#686e81` border, 4px radius
- Value: Lato 15px, 0.75px tracking, `#686e81`
- Floating label: Roboto 12/16, 0.4px tracking, white fill on the border
- Supporting text: Lato 14px, 0.7px tracking, `#858787`, 5px inset — only when the design includes it
- Dropdowns are the same field plus a trailing 24px chevron in a 40px icon button

## Switch

- Preferred control for binary on/off settings
- Track 52×32, thumb 24px, selected track `#1e2743`
- Switch sits to the left of its label; helper sits under the label

## Icon button

- 40×40, 12px radius, 24px icon
- Container is transparent until hover or selected (`#dbdfe0`)

## Tabs

- Lato 15px, 0.75px tracking, `#4b5269`
- Selected tab is bold with a 2px `#4b5269` underline

## Divider

- Full-width 1px `#dbdfe0` to separate unrelated sections

## Menu

- Temporary surface over the field, 10px radius, elevation shadow
- Items use Lato 14px button text

## Section quick actions

- 282×55, 11px padding, 10px radius, 1px `#dbdfe0`
- Options are 40px; selected fill is `#dbdfe0`
